# Environment files. Only bare `.env` was covered, which misses the file
# Next.js itself tells developers to put local secrets in (`.env.local`) and
# every `.env.*.local` variant. This repository is PUBLIC, so an unignored
# env file is a one-command secret leak. `.env.example` stays tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env*.example
